### Feature 3: Signal Engine (signal_engine.py)

Calculate the following indicators in real-time for each active market. Use pandas or pure Python with rolling windows (no need for full DataFrame — use deques/circular buffers for performance):

#### Tier 1 — Core Signals (MUST HAVE):

| # | Signal | Calculation | Range |
|---|--------|-------------|-------|
| 1 | Price vs Strike Distance (%) | (chainlink_price - price_to_beat) / price_to_beat * 100 | -∞ to +∞ |
| 2 | Momentum 5s | Price change over last 5 seconds | Negative/Positive |
| 3 | Momentum 15s | Price change over last 15 seconds | Negative/Positive |
| 4 | Momentum 30s | Price change over last 30 seconds | Negative/Positive |
| 5 | Exchange Lead | binance_price - chainlink_price | Negative/Positive |
| 6 | Time Remaining | Seconds until market close | 0–300 or 0–900 |
| 7 | Polymarket Implied Probability | YES token price (0.00–1.00) | 0–100% |
| 8 | Net Order Flow (30s) | Sum of (YES buy volume - NO buy volume) over 30s | Negative/Positive |

#### Tier 2 — Confirmation Signals:

| # | Signal | Calculation |
|---|--------|-------------|
| 9 | RSI (14-period, 1s candles) | Standard RSI formula on 1-second close prices from Binance |
| 10 | EMA Crossover (5/15) | EMA(5) - EMA(15), positive = bullish, negative = bearish |
| 11 | VWAP Deviation | (price - VWAP) / VWAP * 100 where VWAP is calculated from market open |
| 12 | Volatility (60s rolling std dev) | Standard deviation of price over last 60 seconds |

#### Tier 3 — Edge Amplifiers:

| # | Signal | Source |
|---|--------|--------|
| 13 | Funding Rate | Binance Futures API — positive = longs paying shorts |
| 14 | Open Interest Change | Binance Futures API — % change in last 5 minutes |
| 15 | Multi-Exchange Consensus | Are Binance price AND Chainlink price both on same side of strike? |

All signals must be recalculated every 500ms (twice per second) and published to Redis.

